		(property "Description" "22uF 16V 1206 X5R LOW-PROFILE (GRM319: 0.85 +/-0.10 -> 0.95 MAX), AEM CSRC buffer at BUFSRC (aem10300 Table 6: min 13uF EFFECTIVE - footnote 1 names tolerance + DC-bias derating). Re-picked 2026-08-06 off the height wall (was TDK 0805, 1.45 max): K-tol worst 19.8uF; even -25% bias at the 4.15V Voc worst case plus 5% aging leaves ~14.1uF >= 13. Same 16V/X5R point as the incumbent, and a 1206 derates LESS than the 0805 it replaces. The 2026-07-30 note that 1206 does NOT fit was bounded by SB2, deleted 2026-08-05; refit is the board round. Confirm the exact bias curve on SimSurfing there."
